{
  "family": "motion",
  "spec": "10-tokens/05-motion.md",
  "cssFile": "tokens/motion.css",
  "dartFile": "dart/monokit_motion.dart",
  "dartType": "MonokitMotionRole",
  "description": "Two schemes and only two. Calm for all utility motion — the user should notice only its absence. Expressive springs are a budget, not a style, spent on exactly three moments: a reaction landing, a purchase succeeding, and going live.",
  "axes": [
    "reducedMotion"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "D10: monoOut is the signature deceleration — near-instant launch, long soft settle.",
    "Enters decelerate; exits accelerate and run one step shorter than their enter. Durations are never composed by arithmetic.",
    "D26: motion is roles-only. Per-component raw duration and curve overrides are deprecated; every animation binds to a named role.",
    "One moving subject at a time. Chrome never staggers.",
    "Springs animate position and scale; durations and curves animate colour and opacity. The one sanctioned crossover is the gesture bridge, where a drag release settles on a critically damped effect spring seeded with the release velocity.",
    "D11: reduced motion collapses everything to an opacity fade of at most 100ms, stops loops, and KEEPS haptics — when motion cannot carry the confirmation, haptics do."
  ],
  "groups": {
